+| F03 | Closing can abort after successful save approval | X/S | The actual close function cancels on a changed revision. It also cancels if localStorage.setItem throws after native save approval. Finalize pending editor changes before snapshot; handle a cache quota failure separately from a failed durable project save. |
+| F04 | Replace edits the wrong word | X | Search train in The train arrives. and replace with car: current output is car train arrives. Required output: The car arrives. Store and replace the selected exact occurrence. |
+| F05 | Literal search is interpreted as a regular expression | X | Replace All for . in A.B currently produces ___; [ throws a regex error. Default to literal matching; make any regex mode explicit and validate it. |
+| F06 | Search navigation skips occurrences in the same paragraph | X | train train train is recorded as one paragraph match. Track occurrence ranges, navigate/select each occurrence and recompute safely after edits. |
+| F07 | Scene movement separates headings and their bodies | X/S | Scene List downward move inserts after the next heading rather than after its complete body. Index Cards contains the same formula. Navigator uses the removed scene’s old end index, which also fails with unequal scene lengths. Centralize whole-scene span movement. |
+| F08 | Duplicate creates dangling character references | X | handleDuplicateDocument remaps characterMemory and shortcut IDs but keeps old beat.characterId, tag.characterId, castMembership and custom cast-order references. Remap the full reference graph in every document-copy route. |
+| F09 | File Manager Save As can claim a file was saved without writing it | S | handleSaveAsDocument clones/title-changes the document and writes local backup state; it does not invoke the native Save As operation. The modal immediately announces Saved as. Await the actual native location/write result before reporting success. |
+| F10 | Revert to Saved uses the live autosave snapshot | X/S | handleRevertToSaved reads STORAGE_KEY, which is updated by autosave. Use the correct last durable saved-file baseline or an explicitly selected snapshot; preserve recoverable work before reverting. |
+| F11 | Combine insert-at-cursor can do nothing | X/S | The modal calls combineScreenplayDocuments with three arguments; insert-at-cursor needs insertIndex. Capture a stable editor insertion anchor and perform the insertion with one Undo transaction. |
+| F12 | Combining documents can lose image assets and other references | X/S | Appending a source paragraph carrying an image keeps its source assetId while retaining only baseDoc.studio.assets. Merge referenced assets and metadata, remap collisions and validate all references before committing. |
+| F13 | Comparison word counts miss equal-length substitutions | X | He walks home. versus She runs away. is modified but reports 0 added and 0 deleted words. Compute real token edits, not just differences in paragraph word counts. |
+| F14 | Legacy reformat silently guesses uppercase action is a character | X | A DOOR OPENS becomes Character. Reuse the supported format-aware inference pipeline; preserve or flag uncertain lines and show a review preview. |
+| F15 | Format Doctor does not repair layout spacing | S | Its spacing check currently trims trailing whitespace. Add meaningful template/layout validation and repair without pretending existing whitespace cleanup corrects missing screenplay gaps. |
+| F16 | Backup/recent page counts are estimates | S | fileManagerStorage.ts uses round(paragraphs.length / 28). Use the active measured layout and actual page labels; describe storage destinations truthfully. |
+
+For search and replacement, store the query, options and exact occurrence ranges. Default to literal text; safely support brackets, periods, dollar signs, backslashes, accented text, Hindi, emoji and repeated matches. Navigate and select the correct fragment/offset. A replacement must preserve unrelated words, supported rich text and metadata, update anchors and remain undoable. Recompute stale matches after editing. An explicit regex mode, if provided, must validate patterns and clearly define replacement semantics.
+
+For scene movement, determine each complete scene span by stable heading identity and the following heading. Remove it, then find the destination span in the remaining document before inserting. Use one shared command for Scene List, Index Cards and Navigator, including moves up/down, first/last scenes and unequal scene lengths. Never insert one heading between another heading and its body. Preserve page-lock anchors, scene IDs, beats, cast, tags, numbering and Undo/Redo.
+
+For duplication, Save As and Combine, use explicit maps for every remapped identity and all dependent references. Cover character memory, shortcuts, beats, tag associations, cast membership/order, voice casting, paragraph links, page locks, revisions, images/assets and planning links as applicable. Validate the resulting document graph. Copy owned data deeply where required; do not leave shared mutable state or silently drop source metadata. Disclose unsupported merges before committing.
+
+For Revert, distinguish a saved disk baseline, recovery snapshot, local live cache and named backup. Load the selected correct source and report success only after adoption completes. Preserve a recovery checkpoint when necessary. Native Save As must ask for a real destination and await the write; a local title change is not a successful file save.
+
+For Compare/Combine/reformat, capture the real cursor anchor; show a preview of insert/append/scene-merge results; handle unnumbered or duplicate-number scenes without silently dropping content. Count actual word/token changes even when word totals are equal. Preserve Unicode and supported styles. Avoid automatic uppercase-as-character guesses. A raw-text reformat operation must not silently replace unrelated screenplay content.
